  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Achille D’Avanzo was born in Naples and founded Solido Holding in 1992. He developed the business into an integrated property group that acquires, redevelops and manages assets for its own portfolio and for major financial institutions. The group became known for high-value transactions, including attempted acquisitions in listed property and hotel companies, and D’Avanzo also invested in the consortium that relaunched Alitalia.\n\nSolido subsequently broadened from commercial and luxury property into hospitality. Its Eight Hotels platform has operated hotels and restaurants in Portofino, Paraggi and Cortina, while the wider group pursued the conversion of historic buildings in Rome and Naples. D’Avanzo remains chief executive of the privately held holding company, working with the next generation as the family develops luxury residences and hospitality assets in prominent Italian destinations.",
    "html": "<p>Achille D’Avanzo was born in Naples and founded Solido Holding in 1992. He developed the business into an integrated property group that acquires, redevelops and manages assets for its own portfolio and for major financial institutions. The group became known for high-value transactions, including attempted acquisitions in listed property and hotel companies, and D’Avanzo also invested in the consortium that relaunched Alitalia.</p>\r\n<p>Solido subsequently broadened from commercial and luxury property into hospitality. Its Eight Hotels platform has operated hotels and restaurants in Portofino, Paraggi and Cortina, while the wider group pursued the conversion of historic buildings in Rome and Naples. D’Avanzo remains chief executive of the privately held holding company, working with the next generation as the family develops luxury residences and hospitality assets in prominent Italian destinations.</p>\r\n",
